<section class="sk-section sk-section--indigo sk-door">
  <div aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="sk-shape sk-shape--ring sk-shape--gold" style="width:64px;height:64px;left:6%;top:18%"></span>
    <span class="sk-shape sk-shape--disc sk-shape--pink" style="width:16px;height:16px;right:12%;top:24%"></span>
    <span class="sk-shape sk-shape--half sk-shape--orange" style="width:88px;height:44px;right:5%;bottom:14%;--sk-rot:8deg;opacity:.9"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="sk-wrap">
    <div class="sk-door-inner">
      <p class="sk-eyebrow sk-eyebrow--on-deep">Where it sits in the work</p>
      <h2 class="sk-h2 sk-h2--on-deep">The tea and <em>the blanket</em>.</h2>
      <div class="sk-prose" style="margin-top:20px">
        <p>
          Almost everything we do at Songdance moves outward: you make the sound of what's there,
          and nobody plays you anything. The Songdeck is the one shelf in the house where the
          direction turns around. Here, music is offered <em>to</em> you — the way a friend,
          instead of asking what happened, makes you a warm drink and finds you a blanket. One
          direction isn't superior to the other. They bring different things.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="sk-door-quote">
        <blockquote>
          "It connects us with whatever these words are — if it's bliss, if it's love. That is
          very powerful, especially combined with music. But very different from Somatic Vocal
          Healing."
        </blockquote>
        <cite>Jacob, on chanting and mantra singing</cite>
      </figure>
      <p class="sk-door-close">First the truth. Then the tune.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
